{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-51070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/5eae80c03e35f79eaa484a5d54f7fa1a0ec46a5f27480fb69089efab938eba06.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=-1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-51070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Statement I is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $f(x)$ has a cusp at this point and so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-1$ and so it is not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-51070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f9af49b14e4ed975b26542dcc08e6f8972a92224969edcc797dc30d7a9517cd"} {"question" "q-51070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-51070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-51070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-73252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/1f2d8b9faac6c300b41902cea5065bf8bafb02c137232ee79779a4dc3ff67f33.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-73252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Statement I is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement II is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$ So, it can't be differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III  are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-73252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f9af49b14e4ed975b26542dcc08e6f8972a92224969edcc797dc30d7a9517cd"} {"question" "q-73252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-73252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-73252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-101983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/dc27a54ac20efc84bfbc404a20a91309c60c3fb42118f164129e93eee584437b.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=-5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=-5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-101983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Statement I is false. The function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$ it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is continuous at $x=0$ and doesn't have a corner point, a  cusp, or a vertical tangent.\n\nTherefore, only statement III  is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-101983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f9af49b14e4ed975b26542dcc08e6f8972a92224969edcc797dc30d7a9517cd"} {"question" "q-101983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-101983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/state.json" "file_sha256" "9944d3e008ecdd2117d2486bb933b9a04b0fcd99b361ac922750fc34d4ad75ec"} {"question" "q-101983" "field" "selectio